Disk and memory monitoring
Let's create a small monitoring report.
Create a project folder
mkdir -p ~/projects/devops/resource-monitor
cd ~/projects/devops/resource-monitor
Create a monitoring script
vim mointor.sh
#!/bin/bash

echo "===== SYSTEM RESOURCE REPORT ====="

echo ""
echo "DATE AND TIME:"
date

echo ""
echo "DISK USAGE:"
df -h

echo ""
echo "MEMORY USAGE:"
free -h

echo ""
echo "CPU INFORMATION:"
nproc

echo ""
echo "TOP 5 PROCESSES:"
ps aux --sort=-%cpu | head -n 6

echo ""
echo "===== REPORT COMPLETE ====="

chmod +x monitor.sh
./monitor.sh

This is the beginning of automation used in real DevOps environments.

